# Admin App (`@my-barber/admin`)

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, **static export**, dev port **3001**.
- TailAdmin template: large `@theme` block in `globals.css`, class-based dark mode via `ThemeContext`.
- Path alias: `@/*` → `./src/*`. SVG icons via `@svgr/webpack`.
- Origin: TailAdmin free template (see `ATTRIBUTION.md`).

## Structure

```
src/app/(admin)/           → dashboard shell (sidebar + header)
src/app/(full-width-pages)/(auth)/  → signin, signup (template UI only)
src/components/ui/         → Button, Badge, Modal, Table, …
src/components/form/       → InputField, Checkbox, Select
src/layout/                → AppSidebar, AppHeader
src/context/               → ThemeContext, SidebarContext
src/lib/api.ts             → fetch wrapper (scaffold, not yet wired)
```

## Conventions

- Route groups `(admin)`, `(auth)` organize layouts without affecting URLs.
- Default exports for UI primitives; variant props (`size`, `variant`).
- `"use client"` only where needed (sidebar, charts, forms with state).
- String-concatenated classNames; `tailwind-merge` sparingly.

## API integration (when wiring up)

- Backend admin routes mount at `/admin/*` (not `/api/admin/*`).
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <token>` via `adminAuthMiddleware`.
- Update `src/lib/api.ts` paths to match real backend endpoints before use.
- Follow mobile's pattern: typed helpers, token from auth store, `@my-barber/types` for shapes.

## Current state

- Auth forms are visual templates — no submit handlers or route protection yet.
- Dashboard pages use TailAdmin demo/mock data, not live API.
